  "problem": "If $B={{1},{2}},$ then $P(B)=$",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of $B,$ denoted $P(B),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $B,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $B$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14098182/assets/1043ca38333d8e62100931c1676cba3dc85521134b60b4a5682142618c447cbd.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $B$ are\n\n$$\n\u2205={},\\,{{1}},\\,{{2}},\\,{{1},{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\nP(B)={\u2205,{{1}},{{2}},{{1},{2}}}.\n$$",
